# Summary of changes for run d3ed9fee-84fb-496e-9b37-409eb4b8becc
Completed a full research cycle on **Extremal Graph Theory (Turán / Szemerédi / Kruskal–Katona / Roth)**, producing three sorry-free Lean 4 files under `Catalog/Combinatorics/`, plus the required `FUTURE_DIRECTIONS.md` and `ComputationalEvidence.md`. All 11 theorems compile against Mathlib and depend only on the standard axioms `propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound`.

**`Catalog/Combinatorics/TuranBound.lean`** — Turán's theorem in usable closed form, derived from Mathlib's structural Turán development:
- `turan_two_mul_card_edge_le`: integer bound `2r·e(G) ≤ (r−1)n²` for every `K_{r+1}`-free graph;
- `turan_card_edge_le`: the classical analytic bound `e(G) ≤ (1 − 1/r)·n²/2`;
- `mantel`: Mantel's theorem `e(G) ≤ n²/4` for triangle-free graphs (the r=2 case);
- `turan_bound_tight` and `turan_extremal_exact`: sharpness — when `r ∣ n` the Turán graph attains equality, so the bound is not improvable.

**`Catalog/Combinatorics/RemovalRoth.lean`** — corollaries of two deep Mathlib theorems:
- `threeAPFree_card_lt` / `threeAPFree_zmod_card_lt`: Roth's theorem in density form (a 3-AP-free set in a large finite abelian group, resp. `ZMod N`, has fewer than `ε·|G|` elements);
- `triangle_supersaturation`: the supersaturation (contrapositive) form of the triangle removal lemma — a graph that is ε-far from triangle-free contains at least `triangleRemovalBound ε · n³` triangles.

**`Catalog/Combinatorics/KruskalKatona.lean`** — Kruskal–Katona / Erdős–Ko–Rado corollaries:
- `kruskal_katona_shadow_card`: the textbook single-shadow lower bound (`i=1` Lovász form with the iterated shadow collapsed);
- `card_lt_of_shadow_card_lt`: its contrapositive (small shadow ⇒ small family);
- `ekr_density`: a density form of Erdős–Ko–Rado, `n·|𝒜| ≤ r·C(n,r)`, via the binomial identity `n·C(n−1,r−1) = r·C(n,r)`.

Each file contains `-- !-- Lab Notes -- !--` blocks documenting the hypothesize/experiment/analyze/critique/synthesize loop. `ComputationalEvidence.md` records the `#eval` checks (Turán/Mantel edge counts, the `r∣n` equality cases, and the EKR binomial identity), and `FUTURE_DIRECTIONS.md` lists five falsifiable conjectures, each with a "The key insight is..." sentence and a "Why now?" justification, derived from this cycle's findings.

Verification used full-file elaboration; the three files live alongside the existing per-file catalog entries (the project's catalog is organized as standalone, per-file-elaborated modules).
